## 8. Edge cases & safety rules

- Ambiguous identity → force manual selection; never auto-open (FR-002).
- Failed/pending allergy retrieval → explicit "failed"/"pending"; never "No known allergies" (FR-005).
- Stale data → show "Last updated: [date]"; flag beyond staleness threshold (B3).
- Partial HMIS response → render available panels; mark unretrieved ones "failed", not empty.
- Access denied → show reason to user + write denial to audit log (FR-006).
- Consent absent/expired → hide item, show consent-required state (FR-007).

## 9. Release gate (all must pass)

- **Sign-off:** clinical (panels, fields, staleness, non-device scope) + legal (DPDP, hosting/residency, audit retention).
- **Safety tests:** FR-002 (100 ambiguous, 0 auto-opens); FR-005 (all states + allergy rule); FR-006 (50 denials logged); FR-007 (consent cases pass).
- **QA:** FR-004 (100-item audit, 100% pass); all P0 pass.
- **Performance:** render & degrade budgets met (§7).

